title: Eser Party Conference
subtitle: The PSR chooses their new leader...
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 12 and psr_party_leader = "Chernov"
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/psrcongress.png
tags: event
new-page: true

= PSR Conference

The Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries is holding their quadrennial party congress, this year's congress is expected to be divisive, with the various Narodist factions bickering more than ever after Chernov's decision to step down.

The candidate championed by many Liberal-Narodists and sympathetic Centrists is Alexander Kerensky, the former Government Chairman. His election would mark a turn towards a liberalized form of Narodism, something he has been slowly leaning towards since the Eser's turned to the Liberals for governance.

Our ideal Chairman would be Avksentyev, an Eser who is sympathetic to Marxism and has long been an advocate for leftist unity.

The nationalist-wing of the PSR is calling for Dmitry Odinets, a Nationalist, irredentist, and Narodist who has previously voiced his support for restoring Russia's imperial borders.

Then, there is Boris Savinkov, the man who convinced the PSR to support Lavr Kornilov's presidential run. Savinkov has presented himself as the pragmatic candidate, calling on his ties to Kornilov and to the Western powers. However, most of the PSR is opposed to his candidacy, as he is considered shady and unreliable.

- @kerensky: Alexander Kerensky is elected as party chair.
- @avksentyev: Nikolay Avksentyev is elected as party chair.
- @odinets: Dmitry Odinets is, shockingly, elected as party chair.
- @savinkov: Boris Savinkov is, somehow, elected as party chair.

@kerensky
choose-if: psr_right >= psr_left and psr_relation >= 35
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Kerensky"; psr_relation -= 5
face-image: img/kerenskywin.jpg

Alexander Kerensky has been selected as the chairman of the Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Chernov, with his history of liberal sympathies. He will preside over a Narodist Party less inclined to compromise with Socialists and more inclined to compromise with the Liberal parties.

@avksentyev
choose-if: psr_right <= psr_left and psr_relation <= 65
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Avksentyev"; rural_rsdrp += 5; workers_psr += 3; psr_relation += 5
face-image:img/avkwin.jpg

Nikolay Avksentyev has emerged victorious in the Congress, and is the new SR Chairman! Avksentyev is a "Heidelberg Eser", and has been influenced by Marxism in the past, the feelings of goodwill between Socialists and Narodists appears to be renewed!

@savinkov
choose-if: psr_right = 10 and psr_relation >= 10
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Savinkov"; psr_relation -= 25
face-image:img/SAVVY.jpg

To the shock and dismay of every democratic party, Boris Savinkov, the champion of Conservative, Nationalist, and anti-Democratic Narodism, has been elected Chariman of the PSR in an upset! The Party of Socialist-Revolutionaries is expected to split in half soon, now split between Savinkov's supporters and his many detractors. We should watch his "National-Narodism" closely...

@odinets
choose-if: psr_right >= 10 and psr_left <=5 and psr_relation >= 10
on-arrival: psr_party_leader = "Odinets"; psr_relation -= 25
face-image: img/odinets.jpg

It appears the Conservatives of the PSR have emerged triumphant, as Dmitry Odinets, a Russian Nationalist and Narodist, has been elected party chairman. This is horrible for our relations, as Odinets is a known irredentist and nationalist.